print('Device:', DEVICE)## Product-Focused Image-to-Image Search (Clothes & Accessories)

This Colab-ready notebook builds an image-to-image product search that focuses on clothing/accessories/products in photos and intentionally ignores people. It uses:

- Open-vocabulary object detection to crop product/clothing regions (e.g., swimsuits, thigh chain, dresses, bags), ignoring the person
- CLIP embeddings (OpenCLIP ViT-L/14) for strong visual similarity
- FAISS for fast nearest-neighbor search

Workflow:
- Download your dataset from Google Drive folder
- Detect and crop product regions from each image
- Embed crops, build a FAISS index, and store metadata
- Query with any image (e.g., a woman wearing a pink swimsuit): the model detects the swimsuit region and retrieves similar available products

Notes:
- The detector uses open-vocabulary labels, so you can extend labels without retraining
- CLIP captures color and style well; optional lightweight color hints are provided for re-ranking
